# Infra

Stack (accepted, see `docs/decisions.md`): Docker Compose on the **Mac Mini under Colima** with a boot-time LaunchDaemon (D21, D28); the same Compose on a droplet later. All images must run on **linux/arm64**. ML workers run **natively on macOS** under launchd, no GPU profile (D25, D29). Observability: Grafana + Prometheus + VictoriaLogs + Alloy; Tempo from Phase 5 (D22). Secrets: SOPS + age, `/run/secrets` files only (D16). Remote access: `tailscaled` on the host, optional Cloudflare Tunnel + Access (D17). No MinIO (D8). Read `infra/AGENTS.md`.

## Network

- No broker-facing service, database, cache, or bus is exposed to the public internet. Remote access is over the private network only.
- Bind internal services to the internal Compose network, not `0.0.0.0` on the host, unless documented in an ADR.

## Secrets

- Only SOPS-encrypted files are committed under `infra/secrets/`. Never commit plaintext `.env` files, keys, or tokens; keep `.env.example` with placeholder values only.
- Containers receive secrets at runtime through the secrets interface, not baked into images or build args.

## Containers

- Pinned base images by digest or exact version; non-root users; read-only root filesystem where possible; minimal capabilities.
- Paper and live broker gateways run as separate containers with separate credentials. Live containers are not in the default profile.
- Every service has a health check and exposes metrics to the observability stack.

## Changes

- Reproducible from a clean clone: `make up` must keep working. Update the run/test section of `AGENTS.md` when commands change.
- Backups and restore paths are documented in runbooks and tested by drill.
- New ports, volumes, profiles, or external endpoints update `docs/file-map.md`, `docs/architecture/overview.md`, and the changelog.
